{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Query-Driven Approach and Update-Driven Approach "}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about the warehouse approaches."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Designs the data structure based on the database structures and its characteristics.  Understands the concept of data warehouse, its components and characteristics.  Explains the different types of data warehouse, their characteristics and approaches"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the data validation and data warehouses."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present perfect vs The Past simple: interrogative form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>Both the <strong>present perfect </strong>and the <strong>simple past </strong>tenses are used to ask about situations that took place at some point in the past and may or may not have a relation with the present.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">You can use the <strong>present perfect</strong> in questions to ask for information that started in the past and continues in the present. Use the simple past to ask for information that happened in the past.</p> <p>To make a question in&nbsp;<strong>present perfect</strong>, you need to use the auxiliaries HAVE (I, you, we, they) and HAS (he, she, it) and a verb in past participle form:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Wh-question (optional) + Auxiliary Have/Has + Subject + Verb (in past participle) + Complement + ?</p> Examples: <p><strong><i>Have</i></strong><i>&nbsp;you&nbsp;<strong>used</strong>&nbsp;the update-driven approach?&nbsp;<br />What approach&nbsp;<strong>have</strong>&nbsp;you&nbsp;<strong>used</strong>&nbsp;so far?</i></p> <p>To make a question in&nbsp;<strong>simple past</strong>, you need to use the auxiliary&nbsp;<i>did</i>&nbsp;and a verb in the base form:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Wh-question (optional) + Did + Subject+ Verb (in base form) + Complement + ?</p> <p>Examples:<br /> <strong><i>Did</i></strong><i>&nbsp;you&nbsp;<strong>use</strong>&nbsp;tuning production strategies?<br />When&nbsp;<strong>did</strong>&nbsp;you&nbsp;<strong>start</strong>&nbsp;to work with a data warehouse?</i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Caroline, what domains did you implement for the data warehouse?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You know, I have got to integrate some dissimilar databases, have you done it before? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "What approach have you thought about? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are two approaches: query-driven approach and update-driven approach. Did you hear about them before? "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Data Warehouse Approaches"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>There are different ways to work with <strong>data warehouse</strong>. Some of these ways or approaches to work with <strong>data warehouse</strong> support the work done by executives.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>The <strong>Query-Driven approach</strong> is the most popular approach to combine heterogeneous databases. This approach is being used as integrator or mediator. Some of its characteristics are:</p> <ul> <li>Queries are mapped and sent to the local query processor.</li> <li>The results are integrated into a global answer set.</li> </ul> <p>Its disadvantages are:</p> <ul> <li>It needs complex combination and filtering.</li> <li>It's not an efficient approach.</li> <li>It's very expensive.</li> </ul> <p>The <strong>Update-Driven approach</strong> is an alternative approach. Its main feature is that the information from different databases is combined beforehand and saved in the warehouse. This information is always available for analysis.</p>  <p>Its advantages are:</p> <ul> <li>It provides a high performance.</li> <li>The data is processed and integrated in advance.</li> </ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The query-driven approach is the usual way to integrate databases. This is basically a mediator. Some of its disadvantages are that you have got to do a complex filtering when using a query-driven approach. Also, it is very expensive. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You're going to have to use the update-driven approach since information is integrated in advance and it is always available for analysis. When I used it, I noticed a high fruition when copying, integrating, and processing data. The best of all is that processing data won't require an interface to prepare it at local roots."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "domain "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an area to implement something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Caroline, what domains did you implement for the data warehouse?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tuning "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the appropriate adjustment of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, I implemented data warehouse in tuning production strategies, customer analysis, and operations analysis."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "portfolio "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the contents included in a specific file"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tuning production strategies refer to the arrangement and management of products' portfolios"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dissimilar "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that is heterogeneous"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You know, I have got to integrate some dissimilar databases, have you done it before?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fruition "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to perform an action"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When I used it, I noticed a high fruition when copying, integrating, and processing data."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "root "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the origin of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The best of all is that processing data won't require an interface to prepare it at local roots. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find information about the approaches to integrate heterogeneous databases. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a Venn and Carroll diagram to sort out different and common features among the approaches. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give an oral presentation to your partners in order to explain the information stated in the diagram.    "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about the approaches to integrate heterogeneous databases."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I classify different and common features among the approaches. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain to my partners the information stated in the diagram. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n5le03ob08re2vid01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Steven</strong>: Caroline, what domains did you implement for the data warehouse?<br />"}, {"time": "3600", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Caroline</strong>: Well, I implemented data warehouse in tuning production strategies, customer analysis, and operation analysis.&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "11000", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Steven</strong>: What are they about?&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "12000", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "<strong>Caroline</strong>: Tuning production strategies refer to the arrangement and management of products' portfolios; it is basically a comparison between sales in different periods of times. Customer analysis has got to do with customers' preferences when acquiring products. Operation analysis refers to customer relationship management and analyzing operations.&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "32000", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "<strong>Steven</strong>: I see. You know, I have got to integrate some dissimilar databases, have you done it before?&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "37000", "image": "", "id": 5, "text": "<strong>Caroline</strong>: Yes, what approach have you thought about?&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "39000", "image": "", "id": 6, "text": "<strong>Steven</strong>: Approach? What do you mean by approach?&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "41500", "image": "", "id": 7, "text": "<strong>Caroline</strong>: Well, I am going to tell you what they are. There are two approaches: query-driven approach and update-driven approach. have you heard about them before?&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "50000", "image": "", "id": 8, "text": "<strong>Steven</strong>: No, I haven't. What are they about?&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "53000", "image": "", "id": 9, "text": "<strong>Caroline</strong>: The query-driven approach is the usual way to integrate databases. This is basically a mediator. Some of its disadvantages are that you have got to do a complex filtering when using a query-driven approach. Also, it is very expensive.&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "67000", "image": "", "id": 10, "text": "<strong>Steven</strong>: Have you ever implemented a query-driven approach in a data warehouse?&nbsp;<br />"}, {"time": "71000", "image": "", "id": 11, "text": "<strong>Caroline</strong>: I haven't. You're going to have to use the update-driven approach since information is integrated in advance and it is always available for analysis. When I used it, I noticed a high fruition when copying, integrating, and processing data. The best of all is that processing data won't require an interface to prepare it at local roots.</p>"}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk with a colleague about the domain where a warehouse can be implemented. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe a query-driven approach."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain update-driven approach."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How can data warehousing help in analysis of the operations of a business?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think is the most efficient approach to process information?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "gr